\newlabel{fig:subpupil}{{4}{8}{3D reconstruction of the effective sub-pupils from the Zernike rayfield. $O_L$ and $O_R$ are read from the centre-pixel rayfield. The chief rays converge at the working plane ($WD = \SI {64.7}{mm}$). The baseline $b=\|O_R-O_L\|=\SI {24.9}{mm}$ is an effective rayfield descriptor in the selected gauge and reference scale}{figure.caption.5}{}}
