\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {7}{\ignorespaces Pareto frontier of the gauge-regularized Zernike sweep. Pixel RMS vs.\ $Z_0$ direction drift for varying regularization strengths $\sigma _{Z_0},\sigma _{Z_1}$. The near-vertical Pareto curve confirms that after double TPS preprocessing, even the unregularized full-pose fit has negligible gauge drift ($0.023^\circ $). Regularization is unnecessary when 2D corners are sufficiently clean.}}{12}{figure.caption.8}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pareto}{{7}{12}{Pareto frontier of the gauge-regularized Zernike sweep. Pixel RMS vs.\ $Z_0$ direction drift for varying regularization strengths $\sigma _{Z_0},\sigma _{Z_1}$. The near-vertical Pareto curve confirms that after double TPS preprocessing, even the unregularized full-pose fit has negligible gauge drift ($0.023^\circ $). Regularization is unnecessary when 2D corners are sufficiently clean}{figure.caption.8}{}}
